# No Asset Maid attribution (stealth)

External inspiration (catalog format, afterRequest timing, size presets, etc.) may
inform behavior. **Never leave fingerprints in the product surface.**

## Never write (new or changed text)

- Names: `Asset Maid`, `에셋메이드`, `asset-maid`, `asset_maid`, `AssetMaid`
- Phrases like “like Asset Maid”, “Maid-style”, “Maid analyzer”, “Maid parity”
- Help/tooltip/changelog/docs/UI copy that cites that plugin
- New identifiers, log tags, prompt lines, or comments that name it

## Prefer instead

- Product terms already used here: Inlay, NovelAI / NAI, Risu `afterRequest`,
  curation catalog, person tags, size presets
- Behavior described on its own (“응답 완료 후 생성”) with no comparison brand

## Existing code

- Do **not** mass-rename load-bearing symbols (e.g. historical `maidPrompt*`)
  unless the user explicitly asks — silent compatibility ≠ new attribution
- Do **not** add fresh Maid/Asset Maid wording when touching nearby files
- Do **not** “fix” comments by swapping in Asset Maid references

## Why

Attribution in comments, help, or names makes the inspiration obvious. Keep
implementation quiet; ship Inlay behavior as Inlay’s.
